+++ b/openspec/changes/archive/2026-11-09-fix-sku-case-free-shipping-line-vat/proposal.md
@@ -0,0 +1,31 @@
+## Why
+
+Three reports show the code disagreeing with the README business rules: lower-case SKUs are refused as unknown, an order whose goods come to exactly €50.00 is charged shipping, and line VAT is rounded down instead of half up.
+
+## What Changes
+
+- `Catalog.find` looks products up by canonical SKU (trimmed, upper case), not just trimmed (`src/catalog.ts`).
+- `shippingCost` gives free shipping at goods >= €50.00, not only above it (`src/shipping.ts`).
+- `lineVat` rounds half up with `percentOf`, not down (`src/tax.ts`).
+- Regression tests for each. No README change: its rules are already correct.
+
+README business rules affected: "Products" (SKUs case-insensitive), "Shipping" (free from €50.00), "VAT" (half up per line). All are restored to what the README says; none is altered.
+
+## Capabilities
+
+### New Capabilities
+- `product-catalog`: SKU lookup is case-insensitive and ignores surrounding spaces.
+- `shipping`: free-shipping threshold is inclusive.
+- `vat`: line VAT is rounded half up per line.
+
+### Modified Capabilities
+
+None (`openspec/specs/` is empty).
+
+## Impact
+
+`src/catalog.ts`, `src/shipping.ts`, `src/tax.ts`, tests in `test/`.
+
+## Out of Scope
+
+Any other behaviour, including SKU handling in the inventory module's direct API, shipping bands, discounts, and the receipt/invoice layout.
